  endpoint: "Endpoint",
  apiKey: "API key",
  model: "Model",
  clear: "Clear",
  defaultsTitle: "Default context map",
  defaultsIntro: "Load a saved map, browse a file or URL, download the unique default context map, or save the current canvas map under a name.",
  browseFile: "Browse file\u2026",
  loadUrlBtn: "Load URL",
  downloadFile: "Download file\u2026",
  saveAsEllipsis: "Save as\u2026",
  saveDefaultsTitle: "Save default context mapping as",
  saveDefaultsIntro: "Store the current default context mapping under a name you can pick later.",
  nameLabel: "Name",
  hardcodeTitle: "Hardcode default context mapping entry",
  hardcodeIntroHtml: "Choose a map key to <strong>inline</strong> on the canvas. Every <code>get defaults key \u2026</code> lookup for that key is replaced with a copy of the value from this default context mapping. After that, those slots no longer read the convert-time <code>defaults</code> argument \u2014 they use the hardcoded block instead. The default context mapping itself is left unchanged so you can hardcode other keys later or keep the entry for remaining lookups.",
  importAiTitle: "Import AI suggestions",
  importAiIntroHtml: "Paste the JSON from the AI chat (a raw object or an <code>intehrgrator-suggestions</code> fence). Import validates against the suggestion JSON Schema; errors stay visible here and can be copied back to the AI.",
  suggestions: "Suggestions",
  pasteClipboard: "Paste clipboard",
  copyErrorsForAi: "Copy errors for AI",
  copied: "Copied",
  importAction: "Import",
  notRecommended: "Not on the recommended version",
  bleedingEdgeHtml: 'Prefer to experiment? The bleeding-edge build (updated on every change to <code>main</code>) is always at <a id="recommended-version-bleeding-edge-link" href="#">the site root</a>.',
  newHereHtml: 'New here? Read the <a id="recommended-version-tutorial-link" href="#">tutorial</a> or the <a id="recommended-version-readme-link" href="#">README</a>.',
  dontShowAgain: "Don't show this again for this version",
  dismiss: "Dismiss",
  defaultsBlockAria: "About the default context map",
  defaultsBlockHtml: '<strong>Default context map</strong> is the unique canvas table you author here. At <em>convert time</em>, generated Conversion Scripts receive it as a <code>defaults</code> argument keyed by <strong>runtime key</strong> (<code>language</code>, <code>facility</code>, \u2026). <code>maps_get("defaults", runtimeKey)</code> looks those up. Runtime code can merge that bag with per-message values, other named maps, and Sheet grids \u2014 the canvas map is the reusable baseline, not literals baked into every slot.<br><strong>Scaffold targets</strong> (chips) are authoring-only RM paths, not convert-time keys: <code>Class.attribute</code> (e.g. <code>COMPOSITION.composer</code>, <code>EVENT_CONTEXT.health_care_facility</code>), ancestor paths, and wildcards (<code>*.language</code> lights every language slot). A more specific chip wins when several match the same slot. Empty chips \u2192 a runtime-only key that lights nothing. Extra keys stay available for Map lookups even if they do not light a slot.<br>Confirm, <strong>Apply default context map</strong>, or a later target refresh join <strong>Default point</strong>s. Value edits are live in Test Run. A slot already mapped from source is not replaced.<br>The folder opens load/save: pick a map saved in this browser, browse a JSON file, load a URL, save a named copy, or download the current map as JSON you can upload again later.',
  decisionBlockAria: "About decision tables",
  decisionBlockHtml: "<strong>Decision table</strong> is a named rule grid in the Tables &amp; Sheets tab: condition columns (equality, don't-care <code>\u2014</code>) and output columns (plain values or VMS-Mustache snippets). The grid owns column names and types; this block\u2019s inputs Map keys stay in sync.<br>Plug an inputs Map on the right (keys = condition headers). The output dropdown returns one typed column (\u{1F524} string, \u{1F522} number, \u2713 boolean), or <em>all outputs</em> as a Map (\u21A6). Switching that type may unplug the block; canvas undo/redo restores it.<br>Hit policy (FIRST / UNIQUE / COLLECT) is on the Tables &amp; Sheets tab. Flatten nested sources into the inputs Map (or via variables) before eval.",
